+- **Notes and spot elevations** can be added in them; points run along the line from its start, and up.
+
+### Drawing and editing in a vertical view
+
+- **Aligned or Linear Dimension:** pick levels, grids perpendicular to the view line, or detail references belonging to
+  this view, then click away to place the dimension. Detail-line endpoints can be picked too. These dimensions follow
+  their references; they do not support locks, EQ or typing a dimension value to move the model.
+- **Detail Line:** choose a drawn shape and place its points in the view. Pick Lines and Fillet are not available here.
+- **Move:** select this view's annotations, a door/window in a straight wall, or a free non-adaptive component. Pick a base
+  and destination, or point in a direction and type a length. Shift/Constrain keeps the move along or up the view. A door
+  or window stays in its host; a move off the host is refused. Unsupported selections refuse the whole move.
+- **Trim/Extend:** use the view's own detail lines. Model edges cannot be trimmed from their projected outline.
+- **Escape** and switching views cancel unfinished picks. Ordinary **Undo/Redo** applies to completed edits.
+
+Other model creation/modification tools keep their supported plan/3D workflows. Wall silhouettes and oblique grids are
+not dimension references here. See [[Dimensions]], [[Detail Lines and Line Styles]] and [[Modify Tools]].
 
